README.md:9:Open `http://localhost:8080`. `PORT` defaults to `8080`; `DB_PATH` defaults to `data/workboard.sqlite`. The server binds to `0.0.0.0`. Keep the database file to preserve projects, archive state, tasks, and completion state across restarts. Existing databases are migrated automatically. Parent directories are created automatically.
README.md:11:Create projects on the home page, then open a project to create tasks and toggle completion. Use New project name and Rename project to rename an active project. Names are trimmed and required; renaming preserves the URL, creation order, tasks, and completion summary and persists across restarts. The Task filter shows All, Open, or Completed tasks. The Priority filter offers All, Low, Normal, and High. Both default to All on each page load; tasks matching both filters appear in creation order. Changing either filter or editing a task preserves both selections and immediately re-evaluates matching rows, without changing the project summary. Both filters remain available in archived projects.
README.md:13:Each task row provides New task title and Rename task. Titles are trimmed and required; renaming preserves ownership, creation order, completion, filter membership, and the project summary. Task titles persist across restarts. Each task has a Task priority selector with Low, Normal, and High options. Existing tasks default to Normal; new tasks inherit their project's saved Default task priority (initially Normal). The default selector offers Low, Normal, and High and affects only future tasks. Defaults are independent per project and persist through reloads, restarts, renaming, archival, and restoration. Changing a default leaves existing tasks and both filters unchanged. Archived projects display the saved default but disable edits until restored. Task priority edits persist independently without changing task order, title, completion, or summaries. Renaming preserves priority. Archived projects disable task renaming and priority edits until restored.
README.md:15:Each task row also has Task due date and Save due date controls. Save a real Gregorian date in YYYY-MM-DD format (years 0001–9999), or save an empty/whitespace-only value to clear it. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed. Invalid dates display an alert and leave the saved date unchanged. Dates are calendar days without timezone conversion, persist independently across restarts, and survive renaming, archival, and restoration. Saving a date preserves both filters and all other task data. Archived projects disable date editing until restored.
README.md:17:Each task row provides a multiline Task notes textarea and Save notes. Notes are optional plain text: saving preserves spaces, line breaks, Unicode, and literal markup without trimming; empty text clears them. Existing and new tasks start with empty notes. Notes persist across restarts, travel with moved tasks, and do not affect name/title searches, other task fields, remembered order, summaries, or selected filters. Archived projects display saved notes with both controls disabled until restoration. Database upgrades preserve existing fields while initializing notes to empty.
README.md:21:Each task row has Destination project and Move task controls. Destinations list other active projects by current name in project creation order. A first-time arrival appends after all positions established in the destination, including tasks currently away. Returning tasks recover their remembered position relative to other tasks, even when they return in a different order. Each project's positions persist across restarts, renaming, archival, and restoration; existing databases retain their current task order. Moving preserves the task's current title, completion, priority, and due date rather than restoring old values or applying the destination's default. The source page stays open with all filters retained. Both project summaries reflect their current tasks, and ownership and ordering persist across restarts. Archived projects cannot send or receive tasks; move controls are disabled on archived pages or when no destinations are available.
